Document.description_en:
Ralmax Properties Limited is proposing to install a new barge ramp facility adjacent to 343 Bay Street in Victoria, B.C. Activities associated with the project include dredging and the installation of piles, riprap, winches, and a steel barge ramp.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Transport Canada (TC) is reviewing the project for approval under&nbsp;the&nbsp;Public Ports and Public Port Facilities Regulations&nbsp;(PPPPFR), as the proposed project falls within lands administered by Transport Canada. TC will also be issuing a licence and amending an existing lease to enable the work. Under the Impact Assessment Act, TC is reviewing project activities that relate to physical works on federal lands, specifically&nbsp;riprap installation and dredging related to the riprap installation.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

The purpose of the riprap is to provide slope stability and protection at the base of the barge ramp. Dredging of seabed sediments would take place using a crane and clamshell bucket from a barge. Dredged materials would be transported to an upland facility for disposal. Following dredging, approximately 100 m3&nbsp;of riprap will be placed on federal lands.

Document.description_fr:
Ralmax Properties Limited propose d&#39;installer une nouvelle rampe pour barges adjacente au 343 Bay Street &agrave; Victoria, en Colombie-Britannique. Les activit&eacute;s associ&eacute;es au projet incluent le dragage et l&#39;installation de pieux, d&#39;enrocheur, de treuils et d&#39;une rampe en acier pour barges.

&nbsp;

Transports Canada (TC) examine le projet pour approbation en vertu du R&egrave;glement sur les ports publics et les installations portuaires publiques (PPPPFR), puisque le projet propos&eacute; rel&egrave;ve des terres administr&eacute;es par Transports Canada.&nbsp;TC d&eacute;livrera &eacute;galement une licence et modifiera un bail existant pour permettre les travaux. En vertu de la loi sur l&#39;&eacute;valuation de l&#39;impact, TC examine les activit&eacute;s li&eacute;es aux travaux physiques sur les terres f&eacute;d&eacute;rales, en particulier l&#39;installation d&#39;enrochement et le dragage li&eacute;s &agrave; cette installation.

&nbsp;

Le but de l&#39;enrochement est d&#39;assurer la stabilit&eacute; et la protection des pentes &agrave; la base de la rampe de la barge. Le dragage des s&eacute;diments du fond marin serait effectu&eacute; &agrave; l&#39;aide d&#39;une grue et d&#39;un seau &agrave; coquilles provenant d&#39;une barge. Les mat&eacute;riaux dragu&eacute;s seraient transport&eacute;s vers une installation pour leur &eacute;limination. Apr&egrave;s le dragage, environ 100 m3 d&#39;enrochement seront d&eacute;pos&eacute;s sur des terres f&eacute;d&eacute;rales.

